# The corpus of a set is uploaded byte for byte, and every result depends on
# those bytes: lengths, hashes, where a paragraph ends. With core.autocrlf, Git
# would check the text files out with CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere, and the
# same commit would measure differently on two machines. `-text` makes Git keep
# the bytes as they are committed, which is with LF.
sets/*/corpus/** -text

# Sources the corpus is built from, and the results, always with LF, so that
# rebuilding or re-measuring never shows a difference that is only line endings.
sets/*/sources/** text eol=lf
sets/*/*.json text eol=lf
sets/*/*.mjs text eol=lf
